// An array as a value, methods, kept (a loop): `method int g() { int t = a for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) { t += 1 }
// return t } initial state A do x = g() go to A`. KIELER rejects it: assignment to ‘int’ from ‘int *’ makes integer
// from pointer without a cast [-Wint-conversion].
scchart Main { input bool b input int i int a[2] = {4,7} int c[2] = {4,7} int m[2][2] = {{4,7},{8,1}} float fa[2] bool ba[2] output int x output float f output bool y method int g() { int t = a for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) { t += 1 } return t } initial state A do x = g() go to A }
